course: dictionary
lesson: 10844
title: Vertebra: the bones of the backbone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A vertebra is one of the small bones that link together to make your backbone, also called the spine. The word comes from Latin, but you can understand it from its job: the spine is a stack of many vertebrae.
explain: «The spine is made of 33 vertebrae: 7 in the neck, 12 in the chest, 5 in the lower back, and the rest fused together into the base of the spine and the tailbone.» The sentence tells you there are many vertebrae, and that they are grouped by where they sit. Two or more is vertebrae, the plural. One is a vertebra.
explain: The vertebrae do an important job. They protect the spinal cord, the bundle of nerves that carries messages between your brain and your body. «Run your hand down a friend's back and you feel a row of bumps: these are the back edges of the vertebrae.» Those bumps are the bones you can feel through your skin.
fact: A vertebra is one small bone in the spine, also called the backbone.
fact: Vertebrae is the plural: one vertebra, many vertebrae.
fact: The vertebrae protect the spinal cord, which carries messages between the brain and the body.
fact: Vertebrates are animals with a backbone, such as fish, birds, reptiles, amphibians and mammals.
fact: Invertebrates are animals without a backbone, such as insects, worms and jellyfish.
exercise: What is one vertebra? | A soft cushion between two bones | A type of muscle in the arm | *One of the small bones linked together to make the backbone | A bundle of nerves that carries messages
exercise: Which of these animals is a vertebrate, meaning it has a backbone? | Earthworm | *Fish | Jellyfish | Insect
exercise: «Humans and giraffes both have seven neck vertebrae.» How many neck vertebrae do humans have? | Twelve | *Seven | Five | Thirty-three
test: «The vertebrae protect the spinal cord.» What does the spinal cord do? | It helps us breathe in and out | *It carries messages between the brain and the body | It pumps blood around the body | It digests food
test: Several small bones in the spine are called vertebrae. What is the plural of vertebra? | vertebrate | vertebrs | *vertebrae | vertebras
exam: Which animal is an invertebrate, meaning it has no backbone? | *Earthworm | Snake | Frog | Eagle
